[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615880553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2615880553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2615880553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b6ytp","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T14:16:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T14:16:20Z","body":"I would raise the dots a bit using Normal collision","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615880553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616484886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2616484886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2616484886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b9GQW","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T17:41:50Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T17:41:50Z","body":"> This will crash if [physics runs on a separate thread](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_projectsettings.html#class-projectsettings-property-physics-3d-run-on-separate-thread), check `NOTIFICATION_PHYSICS_PROCESS` in `Node3DEditorViewport` to see how this was handled for similar functionality.\r\n\r\nNice catch, I didn't know that could happen. And thanks for hint of where to look, it helped a lot.\r\nIt should be working now.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5378ed48-2dc4-42d0-a608-a4703cda5210\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616484886/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616543111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2616543111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2616543111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b9UeH","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T18:08:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T18:08:20Z","body":"> I would raise the dots a bit using Normal collision\r\n\r\nThat's a good idea, but it would **have to be a new configuration options to specify by how much**, if any to offset the position.\r\n\r\nThe options menu (PopUpMenu class) doesn't accept an input field to put the offset value there and looking around it seems the go-to way is to create a confirmation dialogue like the 2D snap settings here.\r\n\r\n![_example_snap](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e74b3194-b7a6-43b1-b86c-9722fdafdc3a)\r\n\r\nI think its best this PR just focus on adding the **basic functionality first**.\r\nAnd add extra options on another PR, we can then discuss what other options would be helpful too.\r\nThe waterways addon for example, gives several snap options to chose from\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d02f7e47-d174-44f0-8604-e04bbd1834eb)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616543111/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649820693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2649820693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2649820693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d8Q4V","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T05:20:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T05:20:04Z","body":"> Handling threaded physics adds a little bit of complexity and duplication but it seems reasonable.\r\n> \r\n> In the future, I think it would be nice if \"snap to colliders\" also worked when dragging an existing point. Maybe in another PR?\r\n\r\nOh, you are right, it totally skipped my mind about moving the handles.\r\n**I've made snap to colliders work while moving the handles now.**\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aaf3bf5f-72f6-474b-9bcc-36ad0af26372\r\n\r\nBut it turns out having support for '3D physics run on separate thread\" is proving to be more trouble than it's worth.\r\nThere is not easy way to do it because of how Gizmos work with the 'set_handle()' and '_commit_handle()'.\r\nI've tried a few things but there is no easy way to fix it.\r\n\r\nAnd looking at the addons that re-implement their own path3d like 'waterways' and 'proton scatter', it seems they also don't work with \"Physics Run on Separate Thread\".\r\n\r\nMaybe it can be **considered a bug that the editor itself has physics ran on a separate thread**? The setting itself only affects the editor when you change the option and restart it.\r\n\r\nRight now, I've made it so there is an error message to at least notify the user.\r\nAnd it works as usual, if you don't have the snap_to_collider enabled.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6667cd9b-8f36-4866-bedf-8a7abb1f4668\r\n\r\nI've left the code that enables adding points with physics on a separate thread. \r\nBut I can also remove it to only work with the main thread like before. It's a cleaner solution.\r\n\r\n----\r\ntl;dr: Physics \"Run on a Separate Thread\" is problematic within the editor. Addons tha re-implement path3d with snap colliders also don't support it.\r\nThere seems to be no way to make it work within gizmo's set_handle() right now.\r\nSo I left an error message if you try to move the handles and the editor has 'physics on separate thread' enabled.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649820693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2801480503","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2801480503","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2801480503,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m-zM3","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-14T12:01:41Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T12:01:41Z","body":"I've rebased and cleaned up the code.\r\nI decided to **remove** the half-support for physics running on a separate thread.\r\nIt added a lot of confusing and duplicated code.\r\nAnd there is no way for Godot to execute a raycast inside a gizmo's set_handle when using physics on threads.\r\n\r\nSo a cleaner solution is to just to not allow the snap feature if the editor is running physics on threads for now. \r\nIf there is a solution for this in the future, it can be added later.\r\n\r\nSo for now, I think this PR is done. Awaiting review.\r\n\r\nHere's what it looks like if you have physics running on threads:\r\n\r\n![snap_path_disabled](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b4b809b-0c8f-4f4e-b397-672d22b9ae61)\r\n\r\n----\r\nI have some thoughts about the editor itself being able to run physics on a separate thread, but Godot allows it, and it completely breaks gizmos that needs to use raycast for handles as far as I can tell.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2801480503/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954679166","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-2954679166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":2954679166,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wHNN-","user":{"login":"nargleflex","id":148012087,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNJ8Nw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148012087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex","html_url":"https://github.com/nargleflex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nargleflex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T05:28:23Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T05:28:23Z","body":"Would really love to see this in soon, I've got terrain that I'm using paths to generate collision areas for and it would be really nice to not have to manually align each point in the curve","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954679166/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3515771545","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-3515771545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":3515771545,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RjmqZ","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T09:19:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T09:19:13Z","body":"I've updated the solution to take into account when the physics is running in a separate thread.\r\n\r\nNow this should be ready for a proper review so it can hopefully be merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3515771545/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3833537823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-3833537823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":3833537823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kfyUf","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T07:57:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T07:57:49Z","body":"> If `Snap to Colliders` is checked, and you try to add a point to empty space, nothing happens which is confusing. It should fall back to plane intersection, which is how similar functionality handles it (collision repositioning or instantiating).\r\n\r\nGood catch. I did it for moving the handles but forgot about when creating new points.\r\n**Rebased and fixed.**","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3833537823/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854460719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102085#issuecomment-3854460719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102085","id":3854460719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lvmcv","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T15:39:15Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854460719/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]